# 0029 XeGfxAccel: compressed scanout registry, IOSurface tickets, device-cache accelerator ID, E2 holds, MMIO hooks
#
# Base:  kexts/NVRM/accel after 0002 + 0009 + 0012 + 0024
# Files: kexts/NVRM/accel/nvrm-accel.cpp, kexts/NVRM/accel/xegfx_accel_names.h
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0029-accel-ccs-scanout-surface-ticket.patch
# Build: XeGfxAccel 44aeb7cba2f5 (build/nvgfx/build_nvaccel.sh xegfxaccel; needs core 0028)
#
# Compressed scanout (docs/render-compression.md):
#   - DRM client selectors 9 and 10, WindowServer only: 9 registers a compressed image the plugin made for a scanout
#     surface (surface ID, BO_SCANOUT token, main pitch, CCS offset, CCS pitch), 10 unregisters it.  Up to a fixed
#     number of images, each tied to the DRM client that registered it and dropped when that client closes
#     (WindowServer exits or restarts), not left behind.
#   - a flip of a registered surface points the flip slot at the image's own pages ("xgScanoutPhys") and switches the
#     plane to layout 2, Tile4 + MTL RC CCS with that CCS offset and pitch ("xgPlaneLayout2").  Tokens the display may
#     still scan (the front frame, the one before, one not yet confirmed) are not released, so an image is never freed
#     while it is on the panel.
#   - selector 2's reply carries the flag 0x4 when compressed scanout is on, so the plugin only makes such images then.
#   - debug.xegfxaccel_iop_xe_ccs (1 = on, the default; boot argument xegfxccs=0 starts with it off),
#     iop_xe_ccs_frames / _regs / _fail counters; iop_xe_tile4_plane reports 2 for the compressed layout.
#
# IOSurface tickets: selector 11, WindowServer only, (surface ID) -> (ticket, size).  The surface is looked up in the
# caller's task and its IOMemoryDescriptor handed to the core ("xgSurfTicket", 0028), which makes the plugin's next
# host-pointer import of that surface out of the surface's own memory.
#
# Device cache key: CoreDisplay sets each frame's surface on the display plane through IOSurface::bind_accel with the
# accelerator's IOSurface accelerator ID; the accel's device cache used a made-up ID ('XGDC'), so the IDs never matched
# and every plane change paged the surface off (a GPU copy back to its pages, ~17 ms).  The cache now uses the
# accelerator's own ID.
#
# E2 (early completion signal, still off by default: debug.xegfxaccel_iop_xe_early = 0):
#   - it is held off around every display reconfiguration and from system shutdown or restart on (priority
#     sleep/wake interest registered at start); both earlier E2 failures came at those moments.
#   - the run of distinct surfaces it requires before signalling early is 4 (WindowServer now rotates three scanout
#     surfaces), was 32.  A 11-05 retest with three surfaces still produced hazards, so it stays off.
#
# MMIO hooks: every display register read (nvXeRd) is recorded on the core's watchdog slot through "xgMmioHooks"
# (who = 2), so a read the hardware never completes is named in the hang report.
#
